Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: do not annotate local skbs using recycled RX tuples

The CPU-to-PPE return path has real ingress provenance. Plain local traffic
does not, and its head/tail may still contain a previous packet's RX tag.
Reject it before even reading the tuple reason, not just in the HNAT hook
called after the metadata writes. No skb data or offload setting is changed.

--- a/mt_wifi/embedded/plug_in/whnat/woe_client_jedi.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/embedded/plug_in/whnat/woe_client_jedi.c
@@ -155,6 +155,14 @@ void wifi_tx_tuple_add(void *entry, unsigned char *tx_info)
 	if (whnat && ra_sw_nat_hook_tx && whnat->cfg.hw_tx_en) {
 		struct sk_buff *skb = (struct sk_buff *)info->pkt;
 
+		/* RX tuple fields are meaningful only for received packets.
+		 * Do not mutate a local TCP skb's possibly shared head/tail
+		 * because an old allocation happens to contain a rate-reach tag.
+		 * offload_no_fdb identifies the artificial CPU-to-PPE ingress.
+		 */
+		if (!skb->skb_iif && !skb->offload_no_fdb)
+			return;
+
 		if ((FOE_AI_HEAD(skb) == HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACH) || (FOE_AI_TAIL(skb) == HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACH)) {
 			if (IS_SPACE_AVAILABLE_HEAD(skb)) {
 				/*WDMA idx*/
